      <Output>
        <ErrorInfo>
          <Message>[EventsAcceptanceReceipts] the EF UPDATE was refused by SQL Server error 334 before it ran: the statement carries an OUTPUT clause without INTO and the table has an enabled trigger (TR_EventsAcceptanceReceipts_AppendOnly). The trigger did not reject anything — the statement never executed. Declare the trigger in ApplicationDbContext.ModuleTriggerBuilder with ToTable(t =&gt; t.HasTrigger("TR_EventsAcceptanceReceipts_AppendOnly")) so EF emits the trigger-safe form. Message was: The target table 'EventsAcceptanceReceipts' of the DML statement cannot have any enabled triggers if the statement contains an OUTPUT clause without INTO clause.
Expected: False
Actual:   True</Message>
          <StackTrace>   at WebApi.Tests.Modules.DatabaseTriggerDeclarationSqlServerTests.AssertNotRefusedByOutputClause(Exception failure, String table, String trigger, String operation) in /Users/svendaneel/okam/OkamAPI-trigdecl/WebApi.Tests/Modules/DatabaseTriggerDeclarationSqlServerTests.cs:line 287
   at WebApi.Tests.Modules.DatabaseTriggerDeclarationSqlServerTests.Updating_through_ef_is_not_refused_by_error_334(String table, String trigger) in /Users/svendaneel/okam/OkamAPI-trigdecl/WebApi.Tests/Modules/DatabaseTriggerDeclarationSqlServerTests.cs:line 266
   at WebApi.Tests.Modules.DatabaseTriggerDeclarationSqlServerTests.Updating_through_ef_is_not_refused_by_error_334(String table, String trigger) in /Users/svendaneel/okam/OkamAPI-trigdecl/WebApi.Tests/Modules/DatabaseTriggerDeclarationSqlServerTests.cs:line 273
--- End of stack trace from previous location ---</StackTrace>
        </ErrorInfo>
      </Output>
    </UnitTestResult>
